##### Q6 (cloudflare gpt-oss-20b, v4 prompt, 1 run): In the 2024 Grand Prix race laps, pair each pit-in lap with the next lap's pit-out time to get each stop's pit-lane time. Ignore stops under 10 seconds or over 60 seconds. For each team, give the median pit-lane time and the number of stops. Which team had the fastest median?
== run 1 ==
  step 1 SQL: SELECT
  l.Team AS team,
  median((l2.PitOutTime - l.PitInTime)/1e9) AS median_pit_time,
  count(*) AS stops
FROM laps l
JOIN laps l2
  ON l.Driver = l2.Driver
  AND l.race = l2.race
  AND l.session = l2.session
  AND l.LapNumber + 1 = l2.LapNumber
WHERE l.PitInTime IS NOT NULL
  AND l2.PitOutTime IS NOT NULL
  AND l.session = 'R'
  AND (l2.PitOutTime - l.PitInTime)/1e9 BETWEEN 10 AND 60
GROUP BY l.Team
ORDER BY median_pit_time ASC;
steps=1 ANSWER: '**Median pit‑lane times (seconds) and stop counts – 2024 Grand Prix races**\n\n| Team | Median pit‑lane time | Number of stops |\n|------|----------------------|-----------------|\n| McLaren | **22.887** | 77 |\n| Mercedes | 22.908 | 78 |\n| Red\u202fBull\u202fRacing | 22.928 | 80 |\n| RB | 22.940 | 72 |\n| Ferrari | 23.091 | 75 |\n| Alpine | 23.205 | 71 |\n| Aston\u202fMartin | 23.265 | 81 |\n| Williams | 23.545 | 72 |\n| Haas\u202fF1\u202fTeam | 24.010 | 85 |\n| Kick\u202fSauber | 24.256 | 78 |\n\n**Fastest median** – **McLaren** (22.887\u202fs).'
##### Q7 (cloudflare gpt-oss-20b, v4 prompt, 1 run): Chart each driver's total Grand Prix race points in 2024, highest first.
== run 1 ==
  step 1 SQL: SELECT ds.full_name AS driver, SUM(r.Points) AS total_points
FROM results r
JOIN driver_seasons ds ON r.Abbreviation = ds.driver_code AND r.season = ds.season
WHERE r.session = 'R'
GROUP BY ds.full_name
ORDER BY total_points DESC
LIMIT 50
